  For the clause that says readiness is EXACTLY `{ready, embedding}`, these probes only require the current two mappings and forbid `Pending`. If a future change adds `DenseReadiness::Failed` or any other third variant, the gate still exits 0 even though the pinned contract was violated. Please assert the enum/string vocabulary is exactly the pinned set rather than blacklisting one disallowed member.

- [P2] Match data-migration inserts case-insensitively — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s30/scripts/check-c1-conformance.sh:268-269
  For the NO DATA MIGRATION clause, these `absent` regexes only reject uppercase `INSERT INTO canonical_attributes` / `property_search_index`. A valid lowercase or mixed-case SQL backfill such as `insert into canonical_attributes ...`, or an `INSERT OR REPLACE INTO ...`, would pass this gate while doing the migration the contract forbids. Use a case-insensitive pattern that allows optional insert modifiers and whitespace before `INTO`.
The new conformance gate can report green for concrete violations of the pinned contract. These false negatives undermine the publish-precondition check added by the patch.

